  "prefLabel": "Int 215.03 Waiver by Board",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-12-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Int 215.03 Waiver by Board. The board may grant a waiver or suspension of a rule upon its own motion by providing affected parties with notice and an opportunity to be heard, and issuing an order which finds that:\n\n(a) Waiver of the rule would be consistent with the statues administered by the board;\n\n(b) Waiver of the rule would not injure third persons; and\n\n(c) Other good cause for waiving the rule exists.\n\nSource. #7852-A, eff 3-12-03; ss by #9942, INTERIM, eff 6-18-11, EXPIRED: 12-15-11\n\nNew. #10040-A, eff 12-16-11; ss by #10359, eff 6-14-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/int100-500.html"
